        {
            "_id": "ocYHO8rNnbCQGplD",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Bewildering Hoofbeats",
            "sort": 1800000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The wild hunt horse prances in place, its thunderous hoofbeats creating the sound of hundreds of horses approaching from all directions. Each creature within a @Template[type:emanation|distance:60] must attempt a @Check[will|dc:33] save.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and immune to Bewildering Hoofbeats for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is distracted by the sound. Until the start of its next turn, any time it attempts to use a reaction, the reaction is disrupted unless the creature succeeds at a @Check[flat|dc:5].</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, and the creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Confused] for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As success, and the creature is confused for 1 minute.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
