            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>These fey steeds stand lightly upon puffs of air, their grassy manes and tails swishing majestically in the wind. When not participating in a hunt, wild hunt horses race each other for ever-changing stakes.</p><hr /><p>Although some believe the wild hunt is nothing more than legend, the riders of the hunt are very real, comprised of countless lithe, horned humanoids, along with their steeds and hunting hounds. The term \"wild hunt\" refers to these fey as a whole, as well as to individual groups who gather at a wild hunt monarch's call to pursue their chosen quarry. The less dangerous a quarry, the more likely a monarch will impose rules to make the hunt more entertaining.</p>",
